### 2. UIManager

#### **`G:\git\GitHUb\Unity-GitHub-MO-FantasyBeastStories\FantasyBeastStories\Assets\_Project\Scripts\UI\Framework\Manager\UIManager.cs`**
Singleton pattern with `UIManager.Instance`. Key API:
- `RegisterScreen(UIScreen screen)` — screens register themselves
- `Open(string screenId)` / `Open(UIScreen screen)` — pushes to navigation stack, shows mask if needed
- `Close(string screenId)` / `Close(UIScreen screen)` — removes from stack
- `GetScreen(string screenId)` / `GetScreen<T>()` / `GetCurrentScreen()`
- `IsScreenOpen(string screenId)`
- `CloseCurrent()` / `GoBack()` / `ClearAll()`
- Creates layer canvases automatically with `CanvasScaler` at 1920x1080 reference
- Manages navigation stack and layer masks

#### **`G:\git\GitHUb\Unity-GitHub-MO-FantasyBeastStories\FantasyBeastStories\Assets\_Project\Scripts\UI\Framework\Manager\UINavigationStack.cs`**
Stack-based navigation: `Push`, `Pop`, `Contains`, `Remove`, `Clear`, `CurrentScreen`, `GetLayerStack`

#### **`G:\git\GitHUb\Unity-GitHub-MO-FantasyBeastStories\FantasyBeastStories\Assets\_Project\Scripts\UI\Framework\Manager\UILayer.cs`**
Layer enum:
```
Background = 0, Normal = 1, HUD = 2, Popup = 3, Top = 4, Loading = 5
```
Each layer's `sortingOrder = layer * 100`, screens get `layer * 100 + 50`.

