### 1. CORE BASE CLASSES

#### **`G:\git\GitHUb\Unity-GitHub-MO-FantasyBeastStories\FantasyBeastStories\Assets\_Project\Scripts\UI\Framework\Base\UIWidget.cs`**
This is the base class for all widgets. Key conventions:
- Inherits `MonoBehaviour` (abstract class)
- `autoBind` boolean (SerializedField) — if true, calls `AutoBindComponents()` in `Awake()`
- Virtual lifecycle hooks: `AutoBindComponents()`, `SubscribeEvents()`, `UnsubscribeEvents()`, `OnScreenOpened()`, `OnScreenClosed()`
- Built-in select/deselect/hover animation support via `UIAnimationBase` references
- Helper methods: `FindComponent<T>(path)`, `FindComponentInChildren<T>()`
- `SubscribeEvents()` is called in `OnEnable()`, `UnsubscribeEvents()` in `OnDisable()`

#### **`G:\git\GitHUb\Unity-GitHub-MO-FantasyBeastStories\FantasyBeastStories\Assets\_Project\Scripts\UI\Framework\Base\UIScreen.cs`**
The base class for panels/screens. Key conventions:
- Has `screenId` (string), `defaultLayer` (UILayer enum), `useMask`, `closeOnEsc`, `destroyOnClose`
- Has `openAnimation` and `closeAnimation` (`UIAnimationBase`)
- `Awake()` calls `CollectChildWidgets()` then deactivates self (`gameObject.SetActive(false)`)
- `Open()` / `Close()` are async — play animations, call `OnBeforeOpen/OnAfterOpen/OnBeforeClose/OnAfterClose`, notify child widgets via `OnScreenOpened()/OnScreenClosed()`
- `GetChannel<T>()` uses reflection against `EventChannelLocator.MainContainer` to get channels
- Panels register themselves: `UIManager.Instance.RegisterScreen(this)` in `Awake()`

#### **`G:\git\GitHUb\Unity-GitHub-MO-FantasyBeastStories\FantasyBeastStories\Assets\_Project\Scripts\UI\Framework\Base\UIView.cs`**
A simpler base, less used. Has `Show()`/`Hide()` and `BindComponents()` patterns.

